new.client.tooltip0=Did you know? Mekanism's plastic blocks can be dismantled by sneak-right-clicking with a Crescent Hammer!
new.client.tooltip1=Did you know? Machines with structure upgrades display all available upgrades in the rightmost vertical column of the JEI structure preview
new.client.tooltip2=Did you know? The JEI recipe time for the modular machine Blood Altar is purely for reference; the actual time depends only on Life Essence
new.client.tooltip3=Did you know? Some machines have multiple slices; the structure preview marks them at the top-right, and clicking the bottom-right button lets you adjust the displayed slices
new.client.tooltip4=Did you know? Modular machines can be auto-built by simply right-clicking the controller with a stick; multi-slice machines require adjusting slices in the structure preview and projecting before auto-building
new.client.tooltip5=Did you know? When modular machines auto-build with fluids, what you need is not vanilla buckets (nor almost any IC2 tank), but a fluid tank containing the required fluid; almost all mods' fluid tanks are accepted
new.client.tooltip6=Did you know? Here, Mekanism machines can also use a crafting table to clear NBT
new.client.tooltip7=Did you know? This silly tip is implemented using pure CrT, though it seems kind of useless ()
new.client.tooltip8=Did you know? If you have a wireless terminal on you - even in your hotbar - you can middle-click a block to pull that block directly from AE
new.client.tooltip9=Did you know? The hammer button in the top-right of AE's crafting start screen is also clickable
