novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.2=The Calculation Subsystem introduces §bvirtual Crafting Processors§7 (vCPU for short), accessed through the §bME Communication Interface§7.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.3=§bVirtual Crafting Processors (vCPU)§7:
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.4=  The host provides only one §bvCPU§7 to the ME network at a time, with a capacity equal to all currently available bytes in the subsystem.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.5=  Whenever a user sends a crafting job to a §bvCPU§7, the host automatically adjusts the §bvCPU§7's byte count to the amount required by the job, then assigns it to a §bThread Core§7.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.6=  After assignment, if the system's currently available bytes exceed §e10%%§7, a new §bvCPU§7 is automatically allocated; otherwise §callocation stops§7 until available bytes exceed §e10%%§7.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.7=  As long as the number of allocated §bvCPU§7 does not exceed the §emaximum thread count§7, new §bvCPU§7 can keep being allocated up to the limit.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.8=  A §bvCPU§7 is §adestroyed immediately§7 after its crafting job finishes and §eall items are returned§7.
